# Orvi Feature Showcase

Every v0.1 construct, rendered. Inline text supports **bold**, _italic_, and ~~strikethrough~~ — the same as Markdown.

## Inline visual scope

Colors: [red] red [] [blue] blue [] [green] green [] [gray] gray [] [muted] muted [] [yellow] yellow [] [purple] purple [] [orange] orange [] [pink] pink [] [cyan] cyan [] [black] black [] and [bg=black] [white] white-on-black [] [].

Backgrounds: [bg=yellow] highlighted [] [bg=cyan] cyan [] [bg=pink] pink [] [bg=green] green [] [bg=blue] blue [].

Sizes: [xs] xs [] [sm] sm [] [md] md [] [lg] lg [] [xl] xl [] [2xl] 2xl [].

Weights: [light] light [] [regular] regular [] [medium] medium [] [bold] bold [].

Combined and nested: [red bold lg] red + bold + large [], and [bg=blue] outer background, [bold] with bold nested inside [] [].

Inline links: see [the Orvi repository](https://github.com/jake-w-liu/orvi), and [**the language guide**](https://github.com/jake-w-liu/orvi/blob/main/orvi-language-guide.md) — link text takes inline markup too.

## Callouts

[callout type=info]
  Info callout — a note. This is the default callout type.
[/callout]

[callout type=warning]
  Warning callout — proceed with caution.
[/callout]

[callout type=success]
  Success callout — everything worked.
[/callout]

[callout type=error]
  Error callout — something went wrong.
[/callout]

